{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 22:04 UTC: Smaller checked prudent formula: B(a & (d -> B(F))), depth 2, 7 syntax-tree nodes. Complete depth-1 lower bound: FB cooperation implies X(FB,n)=true for every n, hence X(FB,1)=true. At world 0 FB cooperates with X, CB, DB, so its triple is 111, identical CB. Thus X(CB,1)=true. Every depth-1 box sees the same all-111 CB history for all n>=1, so X(CB) stabilizes C, contradiction. Preparing answer.md; please review before SUBMIT.' >> /work/board.md\nls /work/logs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
